                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8714f5ce-f412-3b04-9669-98da99fa611f",
                        "entry_id": "22402033-f51f-388a-968a-3a8bf6ea9146",
                        "glosses": [
                            "aus dem Mittelmeergebiet stammende krautige, stark duftende Pflanze mit gelblich-grünen Blüten in ährenförmigem Blütenstand"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Gattung"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "47e1a25b-18b2-4f33-8c0b-ad901d4d60fa",
                                "sense_id": "8714f5ce-f412-3b04-9669-98da99fa611f",
                                "text": "Die Reseden sind eine eigene Pflanzenfamilie: die Resedengewächse. Innerhalb dieser Familie gibt es die Gattung Reseda, von der hier die Rede ist, speziell von der Wildform Reseda lutea."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "944ebdf6-1e2c-4ed5-b2d4-7189bf3854af",
                                "sense_id": "8714f5ce-f412-3b04-9669-98da99fa611f",
                                "text": "Und so schlag' ich Ihnen Rosen und Reseda vor. Ein tiefes Grün würde zu scharf hervortreten, aber die sanfte Reseda, glaub' ich, wird recht passend abstechen von der zarten Nuance des Kleides."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4586b020-539d-4533-9080-7cfcc3a0efba",
                                "sense_id": "8714f5ce-f412-3b04-9669-98da99fa611f",
                                "text": "Aber vielleicht haben Sie auch Reseda gern? Reseda ist auch zu haben; schreiben Sie mir nur; und wissen Sie, schreiben Sie mir nur möglichst ausführlich!"
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "2d92a05b-57cf-4710-8dc3-3b7dca470004",
                        "source_entry_id": "22402033-f51f-388a-968a-3a8bf6ea9146",
                        "source_sense_id": "8714f5ce-f412-3b04-9669-98da99fa611f",
                        "target_lang_word": "reseda",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "reseda",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b5356da8-17b0-3785-bd7c-6e1065167411",
                                        "entry_id": "cc9a7454-67db-3b5c-b500-25bbb201c6d2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any of various plants of the genus Reseda having small, pale grayish green flowers, such as dyer's rocket (Reseda luteola) and mignonette (Reseda odorata)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4ac2c465-d70a-415f-919f-fc861ed195dd",
                                                "sense_id": "b5356da8-17b0-3785-bd7c-6e1065167411",
                                                "text": "Reſeda […] An herbe that hath a ſtalke like knots and joynts, a leafe like a nettle, and white in the middle."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "19ac6e14-f27a-4a91-bcc7-08d0ebf61422",
                                                "sense_id": "b5356da8-17b0-3785-bd7c-6e1065167411",
                                                "text": "This genus of plants, of which we have twelve species, was named Reseda by the ancients, from resedare to assuage, because some of the species were esteemed good for mitigating pains; and we learn from Pliny, that the Reseda was considered to possess even the power of charming away many disorders. He tells us […] that when it was used to resolve swellings, or to assuage inflammations, it was the custom to repeat the following words, thrice spitting on the ground at each repetition:— / \"Reseda, cause these maladies to cease: knowest thou, knowest thou, who hath driven these pullets here? Let the roots have neither head nor foot.\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c5fce925-4b57-46df-8ef4-39f0bb048d06",
                                                "sense_id": "b5356da8-17b0-3785-bd7c-6e1065167411",
                                                "text": "A little work on bees which I read some time ago, states that bees collect pollen only on flowers of the same species, in order not to mix the pollen of different flowers together, and I have several times observed this statement as perfectly true during the time when resedas, roses, and geraniums adorned a bed close to a bee-hive. The same bee or humble-bee which had been on a reseda would only visit resedas, another only geraniums, &c."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "66d99b08-e221-3cd4-a942-2502fb14581c",
                                        "entry_id": "cc9a7454-67db-3b5c-b500-25bbb201c6d2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Mignonette (Reseda odorata)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "specifically"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "75c65eb7-302e-41d6-abc5-16ca5020c74d",
                                                "sense_id": "66d99b08-e221-3cd4-a942-2502fb14581c",
                                                "text": "About the middle of this month, if the ſeaſon proves favourable, you may plant out your hardy annuals, ſuch as Marvel of Peru, Sweet Sultan, China After or Starwort, Sweet Reſeda called Mignonette d'Egypt, French and African Marigolds, Female Balſamine, Capſicum, Brown Jolly, and ſeveral other ſorts, which, if artfully diſpoſed, will afford an agreeable pleaſure, after the beauty of ſpring is paſt; […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "63711d2c-1ed0-4bce-b1fb-46d6a718730e",
                                                "sense_id": "66d99b08-e221-3cd4-a942-2502fb14581c",
                                                "text": "Reseda or mignonette is grown in the Grasse region [of France]. The tendency for green notes in recent years has given fresh interest to the reseda note. Absolute oil of reseda has an odour recalling that of violet leaves, but with a rather fine 'powdery' background and a suggestion of rose and a little basil."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "16e73ec6-b8f8-3109-a7d0-00e0241f4fa9",
                                        "entry_id": "cc9a7454-67db-3b5c-b500-25bbb201c6d2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A pale greyish-green colour like the flowers of a reseda plant; mignonette."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fb1be716-f058-4c91-91ed-275be0ab2a14",
                                                "sense_id": "16e73ec6-b8f8-3109-a7d0-00e0241f4fa9",
                                                "text": "This number contains a lis of the manufacturers of tinctorial chemicals to whom prizes have been awarded at the Vienna Exhibition. We find no English name in the catalogue. There are receipts for dyeing wool a bright green; for a finish for pack-thread; for a reseda on genappe; a brown on silk; a printing black on cotton yarn; a blue-black on old cotton, velvets, and velveteens; a chamois and rose on old goods with cotton warps, saffranin on a sumach mordant being recommended for the latter; a black on mixed woollen and silk; a dark green on wool; a cheap violet on woollen piece-goods."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "reseda",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "58b19db8-b656-3306-ac74-0a9abe4db1cd",
                                        "entry_id": "6668f670-72ad-3caf-a894-8fd5ef8155c1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Having a pale greyish-green colour like the flowers of a reseda plant; mignonette."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2d712735-01a0-472a-b42e-3fbd6e33487b",
                                                "sense_id": "58b19db8-b656-3306-ac74-0a9abe4db1cd",
                                                "text": "By mixing a weaker bath than the one indicated the cotton dyes up a dark green, and the wool acquires a dull and weak reseda shade."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4e223a70-0b4d-40ec-89c6-69235bbf3439",
                                                "sense_id": "58b19db8-b656-3306-ac74-0a9abe4db1cd",
                                                "text": "Sateens a 1s. 4½d., 32in. wide, will be very useful, and always look nice, whether as whole or part dresses. There is one of French grey that has a most satin like surface, and another of reseda shade, which is again likely to have a run as a fashionable colour."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "67e23177-27fa-46ed-9aaf-fd6bf6b60928",
                        "source_entry_id": "22402033-f51f-388a-968a-3a8bf6ea9146",
                        "source_sense_id": "8714f5ce-f412-3b04-9669-98da99fa611f",
                        "target_lang_word": "mignonette",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "mignonette",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "39fe1ff3-1a0e-39c0-9772-88c93511ae6e",
                                        "entry_id": "2ce20ca1-6fc9-372c-8571-e9baea4ebdb2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A plant, Reseda odorata, having greyish-green flowers with orange-coloured stamens, and exhaling a delicious fragrance. In Africa it is a low shrub, but further north it is usually an annual herb."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2d599478-8edc-4f84-9e3c-5f34828014bd",
                                                "sense_id": "39fe1ff3-1a0e-39c0-9772-88c93511ae6e",
                                                "text": "After amusing herself for a brief time with picking to pieces some mignonette which filled a box on the window-sill, Marie threw the flowers from her, and exclaimed,—\"And here we are seated together, as we used to talk away half the night in Italy. Good Heavens! how we are altered!\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1c6b745e-2025-4203-a218-8d80911d759a",
                                                "sense_id": "39fe1ff3-1a0e-39c0-9772-88c93511ae6e",
                                                "text": "These rooms were on a level with the apartments of our friends Bows and Costigan next door at No. 4; and by reaching over the communicating leads, Grady could command the mignonette-box which bloomed in Bows’s window."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8d0db3ab-6d7f-35a9-8b45-1ec3ad763514",
                                        "entry_id": "2ce20ca1-6fc9-372c-8571-e9baea4ebdb2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A mignonette tree (Lawsonia inermis), source of the dye henna."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
